Full-screen surfaces must start at the D3D pixel boundary, not its centre.
The host's logical half-pixel conversion otherwise leaves stale top/left
pixels when the scene target is larger than the game's logical resolution.
Keep this correction in the full-screen helpers; ordinary sprite coordinates
and the renderer's D3D conversion remain unchanged.
--- a/decomp/1.9/grim/render/draw_fullscreen_quad.cpp
+++ b/decomp/1.9/grim/render/draw_fullscreen_quad.cpp
@@ -11,2 +11,2 @@
-        0.0f,
-        0.0f,
+        -0.5f,
+        -0.5f,
--- a/decomp/1.9/grim/render/draw_fullscreen_color.cpp
+++ b/decomp/1.9/grim/render/draw_fullscreen_color.cpp
@@ -22,2 +22,2 @@
-            0.0f,
-            0.0f,
+            -0.5f,
+            -0.5f,
